From 4a570e23a759b147d927b1509c1dfdfd3a4b2893 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: huangserva <huangserva@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 09:35:25 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 07/11] feat(tp2): per-unit lockstep between ranks + front
 proxy/supervisor

runtime/engine/tp_lockstep.h: once per GPU unit (each prefill chunk, each
decode round) the two engines exchange, over a shared-memory block, their
cancellation view, committed token count/hash and position. Cancellation
is the OR of both views, so both ranks abort at the same unit; any other
difference aborts the process with "TP2 LOCKSTEP FAILURE". Local
cancellation (boundary cancel, pending-queue drop) is inert under TP.

tools/tp2/tp2_proxy.py: stdlib proxy that starts both ranks, serialises
generation requests, duplicates each body to both ranks, relays rank 0,
drains rank 1, cancels rank 0 on client EOF (stream or not), and restarts
both processes on exit/stall with a 503 to the client.

Tested through the proxy (and in the ninfer-v100:qwen38-tp2 container):
stream/non-stream, no-seed sampling, drop mid-decode, drop mid-prefill,
client timeout, max_tokens, stop, image, image+drop, Anthropic, Responses,
multi-turn prefix reuse, rank kill, rank freeze, forced hash divergence.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
